    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d871">

                <pb facs="0854" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/263</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Danish Minister to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Danish Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-12-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 22, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I hasten to inform
                    you that I have just now (2.35 p.m.) received a cablegram from the Danish
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs advising me that the Treaty for the cession of the
                    Danish West India Islands has been passed by the Danish Parliament and ratified
                    by His Majesty the King, and that the Danish instrument of ratification with
                    full power for me to exchange will be sent to me by Swedish steamer from
                    Gothenburg on the 30th instant.</p>
                <p>I know this information will be gratifying to you, and I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Brun</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
